1
00:00:01,420 --> 00:00:03,380
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:32,050
[wings fluttering]

3
00:01:32,130 --> 00:01:33,890
[YURU] I still remember
the first time

4
00:01:33,970 --> 00:01:36,390
I sensed another person's
bloodlust.

5
00:01:36,470 --> 00:01:39,600
It happened shortly before
my parents left the village.

6
00:01:41,640 --> 00:01:43,480
He must've been a bandit.

7
00:01:44,190 --> 00:01:46,810
My dad took me
deep in the mountains to hunt.

8
00:01:47,190 --> 00:01:49,820
But the one being hunted was me.

9
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:53,860
"A child like you
isn't needed in this world."

10
00:01:54,570 --> 00:01:56,330
That's what I felt from him.

11
00:01:57,660 --> 00:01:59,620
-[Yuru (child) gasps]
-[stabbing]

12
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:01,450
[YURU]
I could feel the hostility

13
00:02:01,540 --> 00:02:03,040
through every pore
on my body.

14
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:05,330
-[Yuru (child) whimpers]
- [YURU] Under my skin,

15
00:02:05,420 --> 00:02:07,540
stabbing straight
through my flesh

16
00:02:07,630 --> 00:02:09,420
and into my guts.

17
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:21,220
[Yuru (child) breathing heavily]

18
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:26,940
[MINE] Yuru! [grunts]

19
00:02:27,020 --> 00:02:28,440
I'm here!

20
00:02:28,900 --> 00:02:29,940
Look at me!

21
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:31,900
Did he hurt you?

22
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:34,320
No.

23
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:36,370
It's his blood.

24
00:02:36,450 --> 00:02:37,780
I'm sorry.

25
00:02:38,620 --> 00:02:40,450
I shouldn't have
taken my eyes off you.

26
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:45,080
[YURU (CHILD)]
Daddy, what is this feeling?

27
00:02:46,460 --> 00:02:48,960
My boy, remember it well.

28
00:02:49,540 --> 00:02:51,590
This is bloodlust.

29
00:02:54,220 --> 00:02:57,510
You may experience it again. No.

30
00:02:58,470 --> 00:02:59,890
It will happen.

31
00:02:59,970 --> 00:03:02,600
Time after time,
as long as you live.

32
00:03:03,270 --> 00:03:04,560
Any time you feel it,

33
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:07,690
do not hesitate to do
what needs to be done.

34
00:03:07,770 --> 00:03:09,770
[Yuru (child)
continues whimpering]

35
00:03:17,860 --> 00:03:19,370
[thudding]

36
00:03:21,370 --> 00:03:22,830
[panting]

37
00:03:27,870 --> 00:03:29,170
[footsteps]

38
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:32,090
[MINE] It looks like
you're a bit calmer now.

39
00:03:32,170 --> 00:03:33,210
Good.

40
00:03:34,670 --> 00:03:36,380
We'll spend the night
on the mountain

41
00:03:36,470 --> 00:03:38,130
and return
to the village tomorrow.

42
00:03:38,630 --> 00:03:40,970
That should give you time
to collect yourself.

43
00:03:41,050 --> 00:03:44,390
-Take a deep breath in...
-[Yuru (child) inhales]

44
00:03:44,470 --> 00:03:47,600
-...and let it out, slow.
-[Yuru (child) exhales]

45
00:03:47,690 --> 00:03:49,980
[MINE] That's it.
Release your breath,

46
00:03:50,060 --> 00:03:52,900
and with it, all the noise
inside of your mind.

47
00:03:52,980 --> 00:03:54,860
-Don't let fear win.
-[breathes deeply]

48
00:03:54,940 --> 00:03:57,570
A distracted mind
leads to a swift end.

49
00:03:57,990 --> 00:04:00,620
Know that on the hunt,
there are lives on the line.

50
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:03,410
Not only that of our quarry,
but ours as well.

51
00:04:04,740 --> 00:04:07,460
Stay calm and assess
your surroundings.

52
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:09,460
Think about what you need to do.

53
00:04:09,540 --> 00:04:12,920
Consider what tools you have
on hand, in the moment.

54
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:15,000
That's how you'll survive.

55
00:04:15,920 --> 00:04:17,920
-[Yuru (child) exhales]
-[MINE] Remember,

56
00:04:18,010 --> 00:04:21,470
death strikes where our fears
make us vulnerable.

57
00:04:21,930 --> 00:04:23,430
[fire crackling]

58
00:04:25,810 --> 00:04:27,020
[MINE] Listen, Yuru.

59
00:04:27,640 --> 00:04:29,060
Don't tell anyone
in the village

60
00:04:29,140 --> 00:04:30,560
that you were
attacked by a bandit.

61
00:04:30,640 --> 00:04:31,860
But why not?

62
00:04:31,940 --> 00:04:34,110
What if all his allies
are lying in wait,

63
00:04:34,190 --> 00:04:35,690
preparing for another attack?

64
00:04:35,780 --> 00:04:38,150
Don't we have to warn
everyone else?

65
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:41,200
No. I'm confident
they won't attack our village.

66
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:42,450
[YURU (CHILD)] Huh?

67
00:04:42,530 --> 00:04:43,780
Do not say a word.

68
00:04:43,870 --> 00:04:45,080
When we get back home,

69
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:47,500
I want you to stay calm
and act like normal.

70
00:04:47,580 --> 00:04:49,750
Pretend nothing happened
out here.

71
00:04:49,830 --> 00:04:51,000
[Yuru (child) grunts]

72
00:04:51,790 --> 00:04:53,960
[MINE] I promise, you can do it.

73
00:04:57,300 --> 00:04:58,670
[bird cawing]

74
00:05:02,340 --> 00:05:03,930
[MAN] Hey, Mine!

75
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:05,890
[MINE] Good morning.

76
00:05:05,970 --> 00:05:07,100
Glad you're well.

77
00:05:07,180 --> 00:05:09,520
We heard you hadn't
returned last night.

78
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:11,520
We could hardly sleep
out of worry.

79
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:12,810
[MINE] Sorry about that.

80
00:05:13,190 --> 00:05:15,860
We wound up chasing our target
too deep into the mountains.

81
00:05:16,690 --> 00:05:18,690
Had to think
of my little one's stamina,

82
00:05:18,780 --> 00:05:20,490
so we decided to play it safe.

83
00:05:20,570 --> 00:05:21,860
You camped out overnight

84
00:05:21,950 --> 00:05:23,870
and still came back
empty-handed?

85
00:05:23,950 --> 00:05:25,950
That's pretty unusual for you.

86
00:05:26,030 --> 00:05:27,580
[Mine laughs]

87
00:05:27,990 --> 00:05:29,790
Happens to the best of us.

88
00:05:29,870 --> 00:05:31,160
[footsteps]

89
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:34,460
[KYOKA] There you are! Oh.

90
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:38,000
Oh, Kyoka! We're home.

91
00:05:38,090 --> 00:05:40,630
Thank the gods.
And Yuru's with you.

92
00:05:40,710 --> 00:05:42,050
[YAMAHA] We didn't know
what to think

93
00:05:42,130 --> 00:05:44,680
when you didn't
come back last night.

94
00:05:45,930 --> 00:05:48,720
Did something happen to you
in the mountains?

95
00:05:49,470 --> 00:05:50,770
Nothing serious.

96
00:05:50,850 --> 00:05:52,980
We let our quarry
get away from us, is all.

97
00:05:58,650 --> 00:06:00,490
Are you hurt, child?

98
00:06:00,570 --> 00:06:01,570
[Yuru (child) gasps]

99
00:06:02,950 --> 00:06:03,950
[MINE] Hmm?

100
00:06:04,030 --> 00:06:05,870
That's the blood
of a rodent we ate.

101
00:06:05,950 --> 00:06:08,030
Boy, I'm hungry.

102
00:06:08,120 --> 00:06:10,500
One rat wasn't nearly enough
for us, eh, son?

103
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:13,160
Where's Nagisa?
With Asa?

104
00:06:13,250 --> 00:06:15,000
Yes. She's inside.

105
00:06:15,080 --> 00:06:16,130
Well, all right.

106
00:06:16,500 --> 00:06:19,050
Let's have breakfast together
with the girls, son.

107
00:06:19,130 --> 00:06:20,300
[YURU (CHILD)] Sure.

108
00:06:21,170 --> 00:06:22,300
♪

109
00:06:22,380 --> 00:06:24,340
-[MINE] Nagisa.
-[Nagisa gasps]

110
00:06:24,430 --> 00:06:26,300
Hi, Mom. We're both back!

111
00:06:26,390 --> 00:06:28,140
[NAGISA] Welcome home.

112
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:30,350
You had me worried sick
last night.

113
00:06:30,430 --> 00:06:31,310
Sorry, dear.

114
00:06:32,060 --> 00:06:34,560
Sorry to you, too.
We were fairly far,

115
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:36,770
so it felt safer
to wait till sunrise.

116
00:06:36,860 --> 00:06:38,270
You weren't hurt, were you?

117
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:40,190
Tell me you're all right, Yuru!

118
00:06:40,270 --> 00:06:42,820
Nothing happened.
Please don't worry about me.

119
00:06:43,360 --> 00:06:44,530
Nothing happened.

120
00:06:45,650 --> 00:06:50,290
Man, I was so nervous out there,
I could barely get any sleep!

121
00:06:50,370 --> 00:06:52,290
Must still be a little worn out.

122
00:06:53,330 --> 00:06:54,500
[ASA (CHILD)] Listen...

123
00:06:54,580 --> 00:06:55,790
[YURU (CHILD)] Huh?

124
00:06:55,870 --> 00:06:58,130
Brother, take care of yourself.

125
00:06:59,710 --> 00:07:01,300
[Yuru (child) chuckles softly]

126
00:07:02,130 --> 00:07:03,550
[Asa (child) chuckles softly]

127
00:07:05,180 --> 00:07:06,430
[Nagisa chuckles softly]

128
00:07:07,090 --> 00:07:08,550
[Yuru (child) laughs]

129
00:07:08,640 --> 00:07:11,510
You should've seen this thing.
It was monstrous!

130
00:07:12,350 --> 00:07:14,060
-[MINE] Nagisa.
-[NAGISA] Hm?

131
00:07:14,140 --> 00:07:16,480
[ASA (CHILD)] I'm sure you'll
get it next time you go out!

132
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:18,940
[Yuru (child) laughs]
You bet I will!

133
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:20,230
-[gasps]
-[ASA (CHILD)] Yeah, and then

134
00:07:20,310 --> 00:07:22,780
-we can have a feast! [laughs]
-[Yuru laughs]

135
00:07:29,950 --> 00:07:31,950
[YURU] Everything changed
for us that day.

136
00:07:32,790 --> 00:07:34,160
Soon after,

137
00:07:34,250 --> 00:07:37,120
Mom and Dad left the village
without me or Asa.

138
00:07:37,210 --> 00:07:38,880
Or so I thought.

139
00:07:39,750 --> 00:07:41,960
It seemed
only I was left behind.

140
00:07:42,670 --> 00:07:44,000
When they fled the village,

141
00:07:44,090 --> 00:07:46,970
they had a basket
containing the real Asa.

142
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:50,050
The girl I lived
the next ten years with,

143
00:07:50,140 --> 00:07:52,310
the girl I believed
to be my sister

144
00:07:52,390 --> 00:07:53,970
was nothing but a fake.

145
00:07:55,060 --> 00:07:56,640
For those ten years,

146
00:07:57,230 --> 00:08:00,150
the people of Higashi lied to me
through their teeth.

147
00:08:01,060 --> 00:08:05,110
Or at least that's what
this supposed "real" Asa said.

148
00:08:06,030 --> 00:08:08,360
But that wasn't
what hit me the hardest.

149
00:08:09,110 --> 00:08:12,120
[ASA] The truth is, I died once.

150
00:08:13,330 --> 00:08:15,580
One of Higashi's assassins
killed me.

151
00:08:15,660 --> 00:08:17,370
[Yuru breathes shakily]

152
00:08:23,340 --> 00:08:25,670
[ASA] We fled the village
in a rush.

153
00:08:25,750 --> 00:08:29,220
People were after us
and the Kagemoris took us in.

154
00:08:30,220 --> 00:08:32,890
After that,
things seemed better.

155
00:08:32,970 --> 00:08:35,810
That is, until Mom and Dad
went missing.

156
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:40,190
Last year, when I was fifteen,
I was captured by assassins.

157
00:08:40,270 --> 00:08:45,520
On that day, they took my life
and I gained the power of Break.

158
00:08:55,030 --> 00:08:57,660
There, as I lay dead,

159
00:08:57,750 --> 00:09:00,370
I saw the boundary
to what comes after

160
00:09:00,460 --> 00:09:02,130
and came upon a daemon.

161
00:09:07,760 --> 00:09:09,470
Half of a pair.

162
00:09:09,550 --> 00:09:11,550
The one with the power of Break.

163
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:17,560
[BREAK]
Lo! New flesh has arrived!

164
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:19,270
[Asa gasps softly]

165
00:09:19,350 --> 00:09:20,560
What's this?

166
00:09:21,980 --> 00:09:23,020
Wait.

167
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:25,940
What happened when I was cut
by that Higashi assassin?

168
00:09:26,020 --> 00:09:27,730
-[BREAK] You died.
-[Asa gasps]

169
00:09:28,900 --> 00:09:32,700
[BREAK] For the first time,
you are dead.

170
00:09:33,950 --> 00:09:35,830
[ASA] Then is this hell?

171
00:09:35,910 --> 00:09:40,210
[BREAK] Well, it is no paradise
by looks, I'll grant you that.

172
00:09:40,290 --> 00:09:42,960
Wait. You assumed
you'd been sent straight to hell

173
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:44,460
now that you've been killed?

174
00:09:44,540 --> 00:09:46,040
Pray tell,
what have you done

175
00:09:46,130 --> 00:09:48,130
that warrants
such self-loathing?

176
00:09:48,210 --> 00:09:50,130
What kind of life
must you have had

177
00:09:50,220 --> 00:09:51,470
in the land of the living?

178
00:09:54,220 --> 00:09:57,430
You stand now at the boundary
betwixt your world

179
00:09:57,510 --> 00:09:59,560
and where the dead rest eternal.

180
00:10:00,020 --> 00:10:01,520
[wind blows]

181
00:10:03,140 --> 00:10:04,810
[BREAK] Oh, come on.

182
00:10:04,900 --> 00:10:07,230
Where'd I leave
the darned thing?

183
00:10:07,320 --> 00:10:08,400
Ah!

184
00:10:10,320 --> 00:10:11,320
[Break grunts]

185
00:10:12,570 --> 00:10:14,570
There. This is it.

186
00:10:15,740 --> 00:10:18,620
This is its name in the tongue
of your motherland.

187
00:10:18,700 --> 00:10:20,700
Yomotsu Hirasaka.

188
00:10:22,620 --> 00:10:25,750
It's like that story
my dad used to tell me.

189
00:10:26,250 --> 00:10:27,840
The village legend.

190
00:10:27,920 --> 00:10:31,340
"The day of the equinox,
a twin boy and girl is born

191
00:10:31,420 --> 00:10:34,550
on either side of the sunrise,
splitting night and day.

192
00:10:34,630 --> 00:10:36,550
They will cross over
to the shadow realm

193
00:10:36,640 --> 00:10:38,300
and learn to command
the daemons."

194
00:10:38,390 --> 00:10:40,260
[BREAK] It would seem
word of mouth

195
00:10:40,350 --> 00:10:42,730
has twisted
the telling over time.

196
00:10:42,810 --> 00:10:46,980
More accurately, it's
"just before the shadow realm."

197
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:49,360
Those people were from Higashi.

198
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:52,150
The place I once called home
tried to kill me.

199
00:10:53,110 --> 00:10:56,070
[BREAK] None arrive here
without succumbing to death.

200
00:10:56,150 --> 00:10:58,700
So? What will you do?

201
00:10:58,780 --> 00:10:59,740
[ASA] Huh?

202
00:10:59,830 --> 00:11:01,620
[BREAK] Those who come here

203
00:11:01,700 --> 00:11:04,080
have two paths
they must choose from.

204
00:11:04,160 --> 00:11:08,210
Embrace death or embrace me.

205
00:11:08,920 --> 00:11:12,960
If you wish to die,
simply take a step off the path.

206
00:11:13,460 --> 00:11:17,550
If you wish to live, accept me,
the power of Break,

207
00:11:17,630 --> 00:11:19,800
and return from whence you came.

208
00:11:20,890 --> 00:11:22,680
I'm quite useful!

209
00:11:22,760 --> 00:11:24,520
Soon as they should
enter your sight,

210
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:26,480
you may part
an enemy commander's head

211
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:28,860
from their body
right on the battlefield.

212
00:11:28,940 --> 00:11:32,570
You will be host unto power
enough to end wars by yourself.

213
00:11:33,190 --> 00:11:36,900
Depending on the age,
you may be heralded a hero.

214
00:11:36,990 --> 00:11:39,780
Break is bound by naught
but your own imagination.

215
00:11:40,490 --> 00:11:41,530
In exchange,

216
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:45,080
you will be set upon by those
who wish to make use of you.

217
00:11:45,750 --> 00:11:49,580
You may find yourself living
in the hell you feared.

218
00:11:49,670 --> 00:11:53,090
You may curse your former self
for not accepting death.

219
00:11:53,750 --> 00:11:56,970
[ASA] I believe hell found me
a while ago.

220
00:11:57,760 --> 00:11:59,970
My mom and dad
both went missing.

221
00:12:00,050 --> 00:12:02,390
I have no idea
what happened to them.

222
00:12:03,060 --> 00:12:04,770
And it's all my fault.

223
00:12:04,850 --> 00:12:06,930
Because I was born, they...

224
00:12:07,020 --> 00:12:08,560
[Asa sniffles, gasps]

225
00:12:08,640 --> 00:12:12,320
Hold on! What about my brother?
Has he come through here?

226
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:14,150
Was he killed?

227
00:12:14,780 --> 00:12:16,190
[BREAK] I know not.

228
00:12:16,280 --> 00:12:17,650
In the event of his death,

229
00:12:17,740 --> 00:12:20,700
he would find himself
in Seal's domain.

230
00:12:20,780 --> 00:12:22,700
He has not been here.

231
00:12:23,910 --> 00:12:26,250
I do not know what's happened
to your brother,

232
00:12:26,330 --> 00:12:28,710
-nor could I find out for you.
-[Asa gasps softly]

233
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:31,460
[Asa grunts, sighs]

234
00:12:34,540 --> 00:12:36,760
[ASA]
Then what choice do I have?

235
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:39,010
We left him
by himself in the village.

236
00:12:39,090 --> 00:12:41,220
I don't know
if he's still alive.

237
00:12:41,300 --> 00:12:44,220
Maybe they killed him,
just like me.

238
00:12:45,010 --> 00:12:48,310
But I have to try and save him!
[breathes shakily]

239
00:12:48,390 --> 00:12:50,520
I can't just roll over
and die yet!

240
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:53,190
[BREAK] What will you choose?

241
00:12:53,270 --> 00:12:56,270
To embrace life or death?

242
00:12:56,360 --> 00:12:57,690
[Asa grunts softly]

243
00:13:02,320 --> 00:13:06,080
[BREAK] You have
the most beautiful eyes.

244
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:08,960
Turn them upon the path ahead.

245
00:13:09,040 --> 00:13:11,000
Never look back.

246
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:20,340
[man breathes heavily]

247
00:13:20,420 --> 00:13:23,010
Hey. She isn't waking up!

248
00:13:23,090 --> 00:13:24,350
No way.

249
00:13:24,430 --> 00:13:26,600
They were the first
in four hundred years.

250
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:28,100
This was our chance!

251
00:13:28,180 --> 00:13:30,560
Maybe this was a decoy
prepared by the Kagemori clan

252
00:13:30,640 --> 00:13:31,600
to trick us!

253
00:13:31,980 --> 00:13:33,600
I know this is the girl
I saw in the village.

254
00:13:33,690 --> 00:13:34,610
There's no doubt about it!

255
00:13:34,690 --> 00:13:36,440
[MAN] Yeah, I'm sure.

256
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:38,480
Years ago, when she was
just a little kid!

257
00:13:38,570 --> 00:13:40,900
And they kept her in a cell
without proper lighting!

258
00:13:40,990 --> 00:13:43,280
There is no way
you got a good look at her!

259
00:13:43,360 --> 00:13:44,780
I know what I saw!

260
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:47,410
Then we screwed up,
'cause she ain't comin' back!

261
00:13:47,490 --> 00:13:49,410
No one's getting
the power of Break!

262
00:13:49,500 --> 00:13:52,000
Don't forget, the boy
is still with the village!

263
00:13:52,080 --> 00:13:54,880
Seal is more than strong enough
to control the underworld!

264
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:57,460
The kid's ours!
He's totally brainwashed.

265
00:13:57,540 --> 00:13:59,960
He'll make
an obedient Seal user for us!

266
00:14:00,050 --> 00:14:02,090
All we have to do
is kill him, and...

267
00:14:03,340 --> 00:14:04,590
[both gasp]

268
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:11,980
[Asa grunts]

269
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:14,730
[both gasp]

270
00:14:18,020 --> 00:14:20,030
[Gabriel grunting]

271
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:23,530
You tracked her down?

272
00:14:23,610 --> 00:14:25,530
-[Gabriel grunting]
-[GABBY] Show me!

273
00:14:25,620 --> 00:14:26,780
[running footsteps]

274
00:14:26,870 --> 00:14:28,530
[GABBY] Asa! [panting]

275
00:14:29,410 --> 00:14:31,040
Asa!

276
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:35,920
[Gabby panting]

277
00:14:40,500 --> 00:14:42,550
[GABBY] Asa. You dummy.

278
00:14:43,630 --> 00:14:44,670
They're dead.

279
00:14:44,760 --> 00:14:46,590
You're supposed to leave
all the murder

280
00:14:46,680 --> 00:14:48,550
and mayhem to us lowlifes.

281
00:14:49,350 --> 00:14:50,930
[ASA] Sorry, Gabby.

282
00:14:51,390 --> 00:14:52,770
If I had any choice,

283
00:14:52,850 --> 00:14:56,310
I wouldn't be a twin
fated to fulfill some prophecy.

284
00:14:56,390 --> 00:14:59,070
But now, I can choose.

285
00:15:00,070 --> 00:15:03,320
And I'll get my own hands dirty.

286
00:15:06,200 --> 00:15:08,240
I'm sorry, Yuru.

287
00:15:08,320 --> 00:15:09,740
You said you were looking

288
00:15:09,830 --> 00:15:11,830
for the innocent little sister
you knew.

289
00:15:11,910 --> 00:15:14,000
I'm afraid
you'll never find her.

290
00:15:14,750 --> 00:15:15,870
No.

291
00:15:16,460 --> 00:15:18,290
She died that day.

292
00:15:27,680 --> 00:15:30,100
So they were an ox and a horse?

293
00:15:30,180 --> 00:15:32,850
Like Ox-Head and Horse-Face?

294
00:15:32,930 --> 00:15:35,640
They look old, but they're
still in great shape.

295
00:15:36,350 --> 00:15:38,770
Seems like someone
really loved these little guys.

296
00:15:38,860 --> 00:15:40,400
[mud scraping]

297
00:15:48,450 --> 00:15:51,200
[Gabby groans]
Man, I'm starving.

298
00:15:51,280 --> 00:15:53,160
Wonder what we're having
for breakfast.

299
00:15:53,240 --> 00:15:55,330
-[Gabriel grunts]
-[birds chirping]

300
00:16:01,130 --> 00:16:03,750
[DERA] Good morning, everyone!

301
00:16:04,210 --> 00:16:05,840
Is anybody in there?

302
00:16:06,550 --> 00:16:09,680
Hey, wakey-wakey,
Kagemori clan!

303
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:12,390
Wait. Is this a call button?

304
00:16:12,930 --> 00:16:16,020
Aren't rich people supposed
to have guards at the gate?

305
00:16:17,230 --> 00:16:18,270
Uh, who are you?

306
00:16:18,350 --> 00:16:20,150
Huh? Finally.

307
00:16:21,110 --> 00:16:23,360
So, you must be
one of the Kagemori!

308
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:25,570
Sorry for bothering you
first thing.

309
00:16:26,070 --> 00:16:27,950
My name is Ryu Tadera.

310
00:16:28,030 --> 00:16:31,030
I believe you've got Yuru?

311
00:16:32,120 --> 00:16:33,490
[JIN] The Tadera's here?

312
00:16:33,580 --> 00:16:35,200
[YURU] Uh, Dera?

313
00:16:36,080 --> 00:16:38,160
Mr. Big Brother
has quite the ride home.

314
00:16:38,250 --> 00:16:40,960
I'd completely forgotten
about Dera!

315
00:16:41,040 --> 00:16:42,670
[JIN] What shall we do?

316
00:16:42,750 --> 00:16:44,340
Oh, uh...

317
00:16:44,420 --> 00:16:46,800
We did forget to tell him
we left, huh?

318
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:49,420
So, yes.
I trust them with my life.

319
00:16:49,510 --> 00:16:51,300
They're a huge pain in the ass.

320
00:16:51,380 --> 00:16:53,850
You don't wanna get involved
with guys like that

321
00:16:53,930 --> 00:16:55,350
if you don't have to.

322
00:16:55,930 --> 00:16:58,430
[YURU] I kinda wanna hear
both sides of the argument

323
00:16:58,520 --> 00:17:00,060
at the same time.

324
00:17:00,810 --> 00:17:01,900
[Yuru grunts]

325
00:17:01,980 --> 00:17:03,190
Very well.

326
00:17:03,270 --> 00:17:05,440
Would you mind asking Dera
to come over here?

327
00:17:05,520 --> 00:17:06,980
I'll let them know.

328
00:17:07,070 --> 00:17:09,320
Akio, escort him
to the front door.

329
00:17:09,400 --> 00:17:10,740
[AKIO] Sir.

330
00:17:10,820 --> 00:17:12,990
No murder this time.

331
00:17:13,070 --> 00:17:15,530
[AKIO] Of course, sir.
I said I'm sorry.

332
00:17:17,990 --> 00:17:20,080
[ASUMA] Good day, Jin.

333
00:17:21,250 --> 00:17:22,670
The manor is a bit of a mess.

334
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:24,380
Did something untoward happen?

335
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:27,460
Morning, Asuma. Nice to see you.

336
00:17:27,550 --> 00:17:30,590
We had a number of external
Daemon Wielders who broke in.

337
00:17:30,670 --> 00:17:32,260
They tore the entire place up.

338
00:17:32,340 --> 00:17:34,890
[ASUMA] Oh, my!
Sounds like a tough night!

339
00:17:34,970 --> 00:17:36,810
And yet you didn't come to help.

340
00:17:36,890 --> 00:17:38,060
Care to explain?

341
00:17:38,140 --> 00:17:39,470
What were you up to?

342
00:17:39,560 --> 00:17:41,020
Just sleeping.

343
00:17:41,810 --> 00:17:43,270
Didn't notice the commotion

344
00:17:43,350 --> 00:17:45,520
with your supposedly
"excellent hearing?"

345
00:17:46,020 --> 00:17:50,490
[HAGURE] Whoa! This is terrible!
What is all this, Jin?

346
00:17:50,570 --> 00:17:52,490
[ASUMA] Ah, Hagure. Morning!

347
00:17:52,570 --> 00:17:54,530
[HAGURE] Ah.
Good morning, Asuma.

348
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:56,620
Do you know what I missed?

349
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:58,330
Was there an earthquake?

350
00:17:58,410 --> 00:18:01,250
Apparently, there was a raid!
A number of Daemon Wielders

351
00:18:01,330 --> 00:18:03,330
targeting Asa and her brother
attacked the manor.

352
00:18:03,420 --> 00:18:05,210
[gasps] Is Asa okay?

353
00:18:05,290 --> 00:18:07,250
Truly sorry
for making you worry!

354
00:18:07,340 --> 00:18:08,500
I'm fine.

355
00:18:08,590 --> 00:18:10,920
[sighs] Scared me.

356
00:18:11,260 --> 00:18:12,380
Wait.

357
00:18:12,470 --> 00:18:14,430
They were after her
and her brother?

358
00:18:14,880 --> 00:18:16,510
Yes. We brought him here.

359
00:18:17,310 --> 00:18:19,470
Oh, you were finally reunited!

360
00:18:19,560 --> 00:18:22,060
At last! How nice. Huh.

361
00:18:22,140 --> 00:18:23,390
Yuru, was it?

362
00:18:23,480 --> 00:18:27,820
Our Asa here, she's told me
so much about you.

363
00:18:27,900 --> 00:18:30,650
These are my brother's daemons,
Left and Right.

364
00:18:30,730 --> 00:18:32,530
[HAGURE] Nice to meet you.

365
00:18:33,490 --> 00:18:35,160
I feel terrible,
I couldn't help you

366
00:18:35,240 --> 00:18:37,120
when you needed me, Jin.

367
00:18:37,200 --> 00:18:39,700
I hit my deadline
and crashed hard.

368
00:18:39,790 --> 00:18:42,370
[JIN] Not to worry.
Good job finishing your work.

369
00:18:42,450 --> 00:18:44,080
But this just sucks.

370
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:45,750
We made the barrier
around the manor

371
00:18:45,830 --> 00:18:48,210
specifically to stop this
from happening.

372
00:18:48,290 --> 00:18:50,630
It does make you wonder
how they got in.

373
00:18:50,710 --> 00:18:52,420
But rest assured,

374
00:18:52,510 --> 00:18:54,050
we'll figure out
after we tort...

375
00:18:54,130 --> 00:18:56,380
uh, interrogate our captives.

376
00:18:56,470 --> 00:18:58,220
[HAGURE] Bummer, man.

377
00:18:58,300 --> 00:19:01,060
Even our own mansion
isn't safe these days.

378
00:19:01,140 --> 00:19:02,890
Gotta sleep with one eye open.

379
00:19:04,640 --> 00:19:06,140
Hey, that's Dad's car.

380
00:19:06,810 --> 00:19:09,150
The old man
finally made it back.

381
00:19:20,160 --> 00:19:21,790
Welcome home, sir.

382
00:19:21,870 --> 00:19:23,160
[GONZO] Yes.

383
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:25,370
Sounds like there was trouble
while I was out!

384
00:19:25,460 --> 00:19:28,460
Salutations!
How is everyone today?

385
00:19:29,500 --> 00:19:31,000
Master, is that...

386
00:19:31,090 --> 00:19:33,260
The name's Ryu Tadera.

387
00:19:33,340 --> 00:19:35,050
[GONZO]
We bumped into each other,

388
00:19:35,130 --> 00:19:36,380
so I gave him a ride.

389
00:19:36,470 --> 00:19:38,390
He's from the Tadera clan.

390
00:19:38,470 --> 00:19:40,470
Seems he's
young Yuru's guardian.

391
00:19:40,550 --> 00:19:42,810
-Holdin' up okay, kiddo?
-[Gonzo exclaims]

392
00:19:42,890 --> 00:19:45,310
So you're the fabled Yuru!

393
00:19:45,390 --> 00:19:48,940
Gonzo, head of this house.
Good to meet you!

394
00:19:49,020 --> 00:19:51,650
And I've heard
of you two as well.

395
00:19:51,730 --> 00:19:54,230
What wonderful daemons you have!
[laughs]

396
00:19:54,320 --> 00:19:57,490
[JIN] The retainers
of Higashi Village, the Taderas.

397
00:19:57,570 --> 00:20:00,530
They've acted as their
liaisons for generations.

398
00:20:00,620 --> 00:20:02,910
Never once has someone
from our clan

399
00:20:02,990 --> 00:20:04,660
seen one of them face-to-face.

400
00:20:04,740 --> 00:20:06,160
They're famously cautious.

401
00:20:06,250 --> 00:20:09,040
And now,
one wanders into our territory

402
00:20:09,130 --> 00:20:11,090
completely defenseless?

403
00:20:11,750 --> 00:20:14,800
Think the Kagemoris and Dera
are in league with each other?

404
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:15,840
Not a chance.

405
00:20:16,590 --> 00:20:19,590
I can feel their
outright bloodlust from here.

406
00:20:19,680 --> 00:20:22,010
The old man and Jin
want to kill Dera.

407
00:20:22,100 --> 00:20:23,890
[RIGHT] What could the Taderas
have done to them

408
00:20:23,970 --> 00:20:25,600
to deserve such hatred?

409
00:20:25,680 --> 00:20:27,020
[YURU] Hey, Dera?

410
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:28,100
What's up?

411
00:20:28,180 --> 00:20:29,600
[YURU] Heard a funny story.

412
00:20:29,690 --> 00:20:32,060
This one told me about Seal.

413
00:20:32,150 --> 00:20:34,360
She said I'll get the power
when I die.

414
00:20:34,440 --> 00:20:36,480
But you already knew that,
yeah?

415
00:20:37,280 --> 00:20:39,240
Same with these two,
but no one told me.

416
00:20:40,780 --> 00:20:43,410
I heard some old legends
the village passed down,

417
00:20:43,490 --> 00:20:45,490
but no details. So?

418
00:20:45,580 --> 00:20:48,910
I've seen you're kind
and caring to a fault, kid.

419
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:51,040
What if someone
blackmails you with Asa?

420
00:20:51,130 --> 00:20:53,000
You'd die for her
without blinking.

421
00:20:53,790 --> 00:20:56,090
I don't want you thinkin'
you can throw your life away

422
00:20:56,170 --> 00:20:57,800
'cause you got one do-over.

423
00:20:57,880 --> 00:20:59,880
It's not that simple.

424
00:20:59,970 --> 00:21:01,510
Get it out of your head.

425
00:21:01,590 --> 00:21:03,470
There's no way for us
to guarantee

426
00:21:03,550 --> 00:21:05,390
you would actually
come back to life.

427
00:21:05,470 --> 00:21:06,600
If you will recall,

428
00:21:06,970 --> 00:21:09,310
you were not the first twins
born of Higashi Village.

429
00:21:09,390 --> 00:21:11,640
Merely the first
in four-hundred years.

430
00:21:11,730 --> 00:21:15,020
One of the last twins
failed to revive upon death.

431
00:21:15,110 --> 00:21:16,190
[Yuru gasps softly]

432
00:21:16,280 --> 00:21:17,690
[Asa breathes shakily]

433
00:21:17,780 --> 00:21:18,900
[Hagure gasps]

434
00:21:23,030 --> 00:21:26,660
Well! Let's not get too heavy
while standing around like this!

435
00:21:26,740 --> 00:21:29,410
So, boy, are you hungry?

436
00:21:29,500 --> 00:21:30,790
[YURU] Uh...

437
00:21:30,870 --> 00:21:33,380
Come to think, I haven't eaten
since last night.

438
00:21:33,460 --> 00:21:36,210
All right! Why don't we have
this talk over breakfast?

439
00:21:36,300 --> 00:21:38,380
It's my treat! Hey!

440
00:21:39,260 --> 00:21:40,380
Tell the kitchen!

441
00:21:40,470 --> 00:21:42,010
We're having guests!

442
00:21:42,090 --> 00:21:43,680
[SERVANTS] Yes, sir.

443
00:21:43,760 --> 00:21:46,260
And I promise,
no poison in yours!

444
00:21:46,350 --> 00:21:47,810
[laughs]

445
00:21:47,890 --> 00:21:50,560
Aw, thank you! Let's dig in.

446
00:21:51,810 --> 00:21:54,520
[ASA] I get to have
breakfast with my brother!

447
00:21:55,400 --> 00:21:57,360
[♪ closing theme song playing]

448
00:23:27,990 --> 00:23:31,160
[HAGURE] I work as a mangaka.
I'm Hikaru Hagure!

449
00:23:31,240 --> 00:23:33,370
[YURU] "Mangaka?"
What's that mean?

450
00:23:33,450 --> 00:23:35,620
[GONZO] Each time
twins like you are born,

451
00:23:35,710 --> 00:23:37,540
the world is thrown into chaos.
